:262,"extent_type":"Small Settlement Area","grid3_extent_id":"35LPH4231_2","adm1_pcode":"CD71","adm2_pcode":"CD7102","adm3_pcode":"CD710201","health_zone":"Kafubu","health_area":"Kinama","name_source":"grid3_names:inside","assessments":[1]},"cod-35LPH5844_1":{"kind":"settlement","name":"Mulapwa","alt_names":"Mutwale","lat":-11.35288,"lon":28.45499,"population":2888,"pop_source":"GRID3 COD population v4.4 (100 m)","building_count":462,"extent_type":"Small Settlement Area","grid3_extent_id":"35LPH5844_1","adm1_pcode":"CD71","adm2_pcode":"CD7102","adm3_pcode":"CD710201","health_zone":"Kafubu","health_area":"Kiwele","name_source":"grid3_names:inside","assessments":[1]},"cod-35LNH5212_1":{"name":"Lubumbashi","population":2605984}},"assessments":[{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"high","basis":"area_report","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Southwestern edge neighbourhoods of Lubumbashi falling in Kipushi territory (Kampemba health zone: Kasapa 2, Iringi, Mulao, La Voix, Kasombo, Mille Collines, Maisha, etc.)","evidence":"Part of the Lubumbashi urban area, policed by the PNC (Operation Ndobo since April 2025) with joint FARDC-PNC cordon-and-search operations against bandits in 2025-2026; no gang or militia holds territory.","unit":"CD7102-kipushi","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[169,171]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Rural villages and mining localities of Kipushi and Kafubu secteurs (Sokoto, Tondolo, Kasangula/Lumata, Kakana, Maksemu, Kinsevere area, Mulapwa, etc.)","evidence":"No reported armed-group activity in Kipushi territory; Bakata Katanga and Twa militia incidents in 2024-2026 were in northern Haut-Katanga/Haut-Lomami. Order assumed kept by PNC posts and customary chiefs, with FARDC/border services along the Zambian frontier.","unit":"CD7102-kipushi","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","source_ids":[176,177]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"high","basis":"specific_report","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Kipushi town (cité minière, territory HQ, Zambian border)","evidence":"Territory HQ under full state administration; insecurity is criminal (armed men killed a court defender and others on 30-31 Dec 2025), prompting protests and a visit by the provincial interior minister promising police action. No armed group holds any part of the town.","unit":"CD7102-kipushi","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[175,176]}],"sources":{"169":{"url":"https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202504110513.html","title":"Opération Ndobo, Lubumbashi - Jacquemain Shabani lance une offensive contre la criminalité urbaine","publisher":"AllAfrica / Radio Okapi","date":"2025-04-11"},"171":{"url":"https://actualite.cd/2026/03/26/haut-katanga-une-cinquantaine-de-presumes-bandits-interpelles-lors-dune-operation","title":"Haut-Katanga : une cinquantaine de présumés bandits interpellés lors d'une opération conjointe police-armée à Lubumbashi","publisher":"Actualite.cd","date":"2026-03-26"},"176":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mai-Mai_Kata_Katanga","title":"Mai-Mai Kata Katanga","publisher":"Wikipedia"},"177":{"url":"https://globalprotectioncluster.org/sites/default/files/2026-03/rdc_clusterprotection_points_saillants_fevrier_2026_2.pdf","title":"RDC Cluster Protection – points saillants février 2026","publisher":"Global Protection Cluster","date":"2026-03"},"175":{"url":"https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202601050086.html","title":"Congo-Kinshasa: Manifestation à Kipushi contre la recrudescence de la criminalité","publisher":"AllAfrica / Radio Okapi","date":"2026-01-05"}},"units":{"CD7102-kipushi":"Kipushi territory (Haut-Katanga), a copper-mining area on the Zambian border just west and south of Lubumbashi, has no territorial armed-group presence. The state controls the whole unit: the PNC keeps order in Kipushi town and in the peri-urban neighbourhoods on the edge of Lubumbashi, with FARDC and border services present along the Zambian frontier. Insecurity is criminal: armed robbery and killings in Kipushi town (e.g. the murder of a court defender on 30-31 Dec 2025 that triggered protests and a provincial response). Bakata Katanga militia activity in 2024-2025 was concentrated in northern Haut-Katanga and Haut-Lomami (Pweto, Mitwaba, Bukama, Malemba-Nkulu), not in Kipushi. The rural villages of Kafubu and Kipushi secteurs are assessed as default state (PNC) presence."}}